cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ZTAP: Zero Trust Agent Protocol"
authors:
  - family-names: McCormack
    given-names: Chad
repository-code: https://github.com/bitscon/ztap
url: https://github.com/bitscon/ztap
version: 1.0-draft
license: MIT
abstract: >
  ZTAP is an open governance envelope and transaction protocol for verifiable
  AI agent work. It defines how agent-initiated actions must be structured so
  they are authorized by policy, verifiable by hash, and auditable after the
  fact. ZTAP does not restrict which agents, models, or tools engineers use —
  it wraps the transaction, not the toolchain.
keywords:
  - AI governance
  - agent protocol
  - zero trust
  - auditability
  - integrity
  - ZTI
  - ZTAP
